    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"LASERGRAPH facilitates printing graphs, created and stored on disk using DATASAVE (Quick, 1988), with a Hewlet-Packard Laserjet II printer.  Graphs may be printed in four different sizes.  The program can be used to construct individual pages or to batch process large numbers of graphs.   Individual pages can be constructed from one or more graphs using an editor that allows placement of miniature reproductions of graphs on a scale model of an 8.5 x 11 inch page.   The editor may also be used to create page formats that control batch plotting of the graphs stored on a single disk.\"",
